WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.260
Princess Leia's journey from an orphaned prisoner
of the Empire into a kickass space general

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.110
has been nothing short of stellar to watch
over the decades.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:09.990
"Somebody has to save our skins.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.520
Into the garbage chute, flyboy."

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.460
But the history behind the Star Wars character
is a fascinating galaxy unto itself.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.640
Here's the untold truth of Princess Leia.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.520
A symbol of hope

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.920
Star Wars creator George Lucas developed many
of the franchise characters' names based on

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.590
their phonetic pleasantry — how good they
feel to say and to hear — and a determination

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.440
to steer clear from some of the more common
sci-fi naming conventions.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.140
But for Leia Organa, he took things a step
further: Her name is a play on Princess Dejah

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.300
Thoris from Edgar Rice Burroughs' John Carter
of Mars stories, combined with Lady Galadriel

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.329
from J.R.R Tolkien's Lord of the Rings.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:52.700
Dejah, Galadriel, Leia … sounds about right.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.989
Meanwhile, Organa comes from a more obvious
source, as it's meant to sound like the word

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:01.809
"organic," as a nod to the fact that Leia
and her rebels represent a more natural, life-loving

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:05.120
side of things than the Death Star-wielding
Empire.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.570
The hairstyle

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.310
Few have ever been able to lay claim to a
fashion moment as their own as much as Leia

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.420
and her cinnamon bun-style hairdo.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.630
Interestingly enough, however — that hemispherical
hair almost didn't make it into the movie

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:17.820
in the first place.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.890
The original concept artwork for Leia had
no such hairstyle drawn in, but Lucas landed

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.650
on the look as a tribute to 20th century Mexican
revolutionary women.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:31.479
He told Time Magazine that he wanted to capture
"a kind of Southwestern Pancho Villa woman

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:35.710
revolutionary look … the buns are basically
from turn-of-the-century Mexico."

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:40.450
Unfortunately, historians have since stepped
forward to dispute his characterization of

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:45.340
that era, but there was reportedly an Arizonian
tribe of women called the Hopi who wore their

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:48.130
hair in a similar fashion around the 1920s.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:53.450
Perhaps not coincidentally, the cultural adoption
of the Hopis' "squash blossom" style by non-tribal

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:58.340
women of the era was seen as an act of rebellion
and feminism for splitting from the mainstream

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.340
style.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.430
"I don't know who you are or where you came
from, but from now on you do as I tell you."

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:09.080
Decades later, Fisher's own daughter Billie
Lourd wore earmuffs on Scream Queens as a

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.120
subtle tribute to her mom's iconic look.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.420
The twins

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.790
Some Star Wars fans still have trouble watching
the scene in Empire Strikes Back when Leia

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.830
plants a smooch on her secret brother Luke
Skywalker.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.790
Even though the two didn't know they were
related until Return of the Jedi, it still

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.840
doesn't sit very well knowing what we know
from later in the series, and Mark Hamill

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.950
himself has said it had a lasting impact on
the character.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.450
This has, naturally, drummed up some questions
about whether the two were originally intended

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.660
to be sister and brother in the first place.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:43.420
Rumor has it that in the original draft for
Empire Strikes Back, Luke's sister was actually

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.050
named Nellith.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.300
Ladies first

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.930
When Star Wars first debuted in 1977, Princess
Leia was among the first film toys that kids

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.550
got to place on their shelves.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.360
"Princess Leia, champion of the rebel cause."

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.740
The company that made the original action
figures for the series released a set of four

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.900
figures: Luke, R2-D2, Chewbacca, and Princess
Leia, who wielded her own blaster, too.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:12.610
That meant that Leia figures predated both
Han Solo and Darth Vader in collectability

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.959
and that she was recognized as more than just
some damsel in distress from the get-go.

00:03:17.959 --> 00:03:19.209
Costuming gripes

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:23.280
Carrie Fisher was undoubtedly the lifeblood
that made Leia so special on-screen.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.890
"It was me.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.069
I don't want to brag or anything, you know."

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:30.980
So, it should come as little surprise that,
like her counterpart, Fisher became known

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.390
as being a bit rebellious.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:37.120
Her wit and resistance to being labeled as
a sexpot was also a mainstay of her post-Star

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.120
Wars fame.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.120
And she was particularly outspoken about the
challenges of some of Leia's costumes.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:47.090
For example, Fisher revealed in her comedic
stand-up special-turned-memoir Wishful Drinking

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:52.170
that George Lucas instructed her not to wear
a bra under her infamous white dress because,

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.349
to his mind, women in space wouldn't wear
underwear...for fear that they'd be strangled

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:58.450
in zero gravity situations.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:03.400
The infamous gold bikini Leia wore while imprisoned
by Jabba the Hutt during Return of the Jedi

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.540
was also a subject of some discord with Fisher,
who kindly advised The Force Awakens actress

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.090
Daisy Ridley to resist a similar fate.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:14.980
However, Fisher ultimately made peace with
the costume by creating her own backstory

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:15.980
for the look.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.109
In response to a citizen movement to have
"slave Leia" items removed from Star Wars

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:24.160
merchandise, she said, "To the father who
flipped out about it, 'What am I going to

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.009
tell my kid about why she's in that outfit?'

00:04:26.009 --> 00:04:29.699
Tell them that a giant slug captured me and
forced me to wear that stupid outfit, and

00:04:29.699 --> 00:04:31.409
then I killed him because I didn't like it.

00:04:31.409 --> 00:04:32.729
And then I took it off.

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:33.729
Backstage."

00:04:33.729 --> 00:04:35.509
Leia in real life

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:40.550
In Fisher's final memoir, The Princess Diarist,
she revealed the intense love affair she and

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.240
Han Solo actor Harrison Ford engaged in during
filming — and how it bled into the movie

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.240
itself.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.819
She explained in 2016 that the pair had a
wild night out with the cast of Monty Python

00:04:50.819 --> 00:04:55.520
and the Rolling Stones that included a spirits
concoction called the "Tunisian Death Drink"

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.879
and kept them up all night until their call
time the next day for the Cloud City scene.

00:04:59.879 --> 00:05:02.349
Their smiles were there for a reason.

00:05:02.349 --> 00:05:03.779
Bonus spirit

00:05:03.779 --> 00:05:08.819
Shortly after Fisher's unexpected passing
in late 2016, a deleted scene from The Force

00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:13.379
Awakens went viral due to its epic display
of the character's grit and wit in the matter

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.849
of just a few sentences.

00:05:14.849 --> 00:05:19.350
"Not all the senators think I'm insane, or
maybe they do.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.509
I don't care."

00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:24.750
For many, the moment was a perfect example
of Leia's growth and tenacity throughout the

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.889
series, bookending her unending willingness
to fight for the Republic.

00:05:28.889 --> 00:05:30.360
She's one with the Force?

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:34.189
There's another question that's long irked
audiences of the Star Wars series.

00:05:34.189 --> 00:05:39.080
Why didn't Leia, who was not only Force-sensitive
but strong, ever become a Jedi herself?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.409
According to The Force Awakens director J.J.
Abrams, though, it was a mere matter of the

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.979
character's own "choice."

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:49.770
He explained that it was a topic of conversation
between himself, Lucas, and Fisher during

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:54.330
the development of Episode 7 and that they
all decided that while there was no age limit

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.550
at which a person could be trained as a Jedi
Knight, "It was simply a choice [Leia] made,

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:03.289
that her decision to run the Rebellion, and
ultimately this resistance, and consider herself

00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:08.240
a General as opposed to a Jedi, was simply
a choice that she took … she's still Force-strong.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.560
And it's something that I think is an intrinsic
piece of her character."

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.770
Making it her call all along certainly seems
fitting for the Princess — nay, General.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.149
"May the Force Be With You"

00:06:19.149 --> 00:06:20.849
Thanks for watching!

00:06:20.849 --> 00:06:23.449
